<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - Del Monte H1 shr drops, no div.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Del Monte H1 shr drops, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended May 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr, (cts)</p>
<p>    - headline		11.7	  vs 17.8</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 None	  vs 7.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   40.09	 vs 60.82</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   78.96	 vs 96.71</p>
<p>    Tax			 7.18	  vs 17.59</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   55.44	 vs 58.38</p>
<p>    Turnover		  1,551.78    vs 1,454.60</p>
<p>Full name: Del Monte Royal Foods Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - In view of the need to retain cash within the group, the company said it was not paying a dividend and did not expect to pay a final dividend. Del Monte will transfer 1.6 billion rand from its share premium account to cover restructuring costs of 360 million rand, a 1.2 billion rand write down of trademarks and the write off of 50 million in premium on the acquisition of subsidiaries.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected a fall in earnings but most declined to predict figures after the firm recently issued a profit warning.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
